UPDATE 2026-09-06 (seat06): ROOT-CAUSED via ASM-diff, routed to hq_B. The first divergence (a variable
holding a co-expression displays as `c : ""` under SCRIP where real icont/iconx prints
`c : co-expression_2(0)`) is `bb_create()` (src/templates/bb/bb_create.cpp:27-28) writing only the low 8
of the 16-byte DESCR_t result slot -- the high 8 bytes (the payload union) are left as uninitialized stack
garbage, confirmed non-deterministic across source texts (a second minimal witness read back `"ARRAY"`
instead of `""`) but reproducible per fixed compiled program. Co-expressions have no dedicated descriptor
tag anywhere in descr.h, which is why this only breaks generic value flow (image/type/copy/list-storage)
and not create+activate, which privately agree on a bare-pointer convention. Full trace, the wider gap
(no per-instance id or results-produced counter either), and the fix shape: see
icon-coexpression-create-writes-only-8-of-16-descriptor-bytes-corrupting-the-type-tag (rank 2, hq_B).
Not yet checked for further divergences in this file past the first one (per this row's own "one witness
per class, don't batch-assume" method -- stop at the first line, classify, move on); this marker stays
until the new row lands AND the rest of case.icn is re-verified end-to-end.
